                        "sense_id": "b55dc8e2-fb8c-381c-bec0-52e8329b8d79",
                        "entry_id": "44598428-c8d0-37ac-982d-9e7f3be89ec7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The muscular system of an animal, or of any of its parts"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "64cf3376-c198-4f1a-8ea9-11ef09182d03",
                                "sense_id": "b55dc8e2-fb8c-381c-bec0-52e8329b8d79",
                                "text": "This would not be the proper place for entering into an exhaustive account of the musculation of the Tyroglyphidæ; which would necessarily be lengthy , and would probably be of comparatively littel interest to most readers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2991a4ad-b561-4aab-9b9e-783dba7e1376",
                                "sense_id": "b55dc8e2-fb8c-381c-bec0-52e8329b8d79",
                                "text": "The main difference of it from Sokolov's scheme is the presence of dermal musculation and the specific features of the outer layers' structure,"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                        "entry_id": "44598428-c8d0-37ac-982d-9e7f3be89ec7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The use of muscles; muscular activity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eca87f4a-98c1-426a-a0c9-d98879bccbe0",
                                "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                                "text": "Will has two provinces, musculaltion and attention."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d415fc5c-5a3b-45d1-abd2-225768118be8",
                                "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                                "text": "For the muscle elements, being thus sustained by electrical force, and operated by electrical force, friction and strain during musculation are made impossible, a perpetual balance in force, which it necessarily involves, making it impossible."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45ab27bc-29fb-494f-a0a8-82d42a503682",
                                "sense_id": "2cf435a2-4ec4-3827-865e-35925ce83718",
                                "text": "Whatever may be the remote causes of vocal defects, the direct cause is always a faulty musculation in the vocal mechanism. The method of training hitherto used to correct this faulty musculation has been for the most part an indirect one."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
